@include ../../shared/squash.overtone

## Backhand length by height
Backhand length by height, three minutes. Behind the short line, a racket length off the side wall.
Straight drives at medium pace, aimed about a racket head above the service line. Height gives you
length without forcing it: first bounce behind the service box, second bounce near the back wall.
When a good one dies in the back, play the next one higher and softer to get the rally back.
+0:00.5 [countdown]
--- 3:00
0:00 [go]
8% Aim higher, not harder.
33% Racket away from your body. Rotate.
58% Hit it level with your front foot. Weight goes forward.
78% Finish high, to the front wall. Keep the grip relaxed.
-0:10 Ten seconds.
---
[stop]
